A multi-line English string with SQL trigger words keeps its line
breaks byte for byte (issue #82). Kept at column 0: a non-SQL multi-line
string inside an indented block trips a range-formatting bug (see the
suite report), so this input stays top-level.
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE sMsg;
sMsg := "Select the samples from the rack
and update the status column";
-- format --
:DECLARE sMsg;
sMsg := "Select the samples from the rack
and update the status column";
-- diagnostics --
